nd user data privacy. arXiv is committed to these values and only works with partners that adhere to them.\nL157: Have an idea for a project that will add value for arXiv's community? cite53†Learn more about arXivLabs†info.arxiv.org .\nL158: \nL159: cite54†Which authors of this paper are endorsers? | Disable MathJax (cite55†What is MathJax?†info.arxiv.org )\nL160: \nL161: We gratefully acknowledge support from our major funders, cite56†member institutions†info.arxiv.org , , and all contributors.\nL162: cite57†About†info.arxiv.org · cite58†Help†info.arxiv.org · cite59†Contact†info.arxiv.org · cite60†Subscribe†info.arxiv.org · cite61†Copyright†info.arxiv.org · cite62†Privacy†info.arxiv.org · cite63†Accessibility†info.arxiv.org · cite64†Operational Status (opens in new tab)†status.arxiv.org L163: \nL164: Major funding support from\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n[2507.16075v1] Deep Researcher with Test-Time Diffusion (https://arxiv.org/abs/2507.16075v1)\nciteturn3370view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2507.16075v1\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 159\nL0: cite0†Search cite1†Submit cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite3†Log in L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Computer Science > Computation and Language\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 21 Jul 2025]\nL9: # Title:Deep Researcher with Test-Time Diffusion\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite5†Rujun Han , cite6†Yanfei Chen , cite7†Zoey CuiZhu , cite8†Lesly Miculicich , cite9†Guan Sun , cite10†Yuanjun Bi , cite11†Weiming Wen , cite12†Hui Wan , cite13†Chunfeng Wen , cite14†Solène Maître , cite15†George Lee , cite16†Vishy Tirumalashetty , cite17†Emily Xue , cite18†Zizhao Zhang , cite19†Salem Haykal , cite20†Burak Gokturk , cite21†Tomas Pfister , cite22†Chen-Yu Lee L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled Deep Researcher with Test-Time Diffusion, by Rujun Han and 17 other authors\nL14: cite23†View PDF cite24†HTML (experimental) L15: > Abstract:Deep research agents, powered by Large Language Models (LLMs), are rapidly advancing; yet, their performance often plateaus when generating complex, long-form research reports using generic test-time scaling algorithms. Drawing inspiration from the iterative nature of human research, which involves cycles of searching, reasoning, and revision, we propose the Test-Time Diffusion Deep Researcher (TTD-DR). This novel framework conceptualizes research report generation as a diffusion process.\nL16: TTD-DR initiates this process with a preliminary draft, an updatable skeleton that serves as an evolving foundation to guide the research direction. The draft is then iteratively refined through a \"denoising\" process, which is dynamically informed by a retrieval mechanism that incorporates external information at each step.\nL17: The core process is further enhanced by a self-evolutionary algorithm applied to each component of the agentic workflow, ensuring the generation of high-quality context for the diffusion process. This draft-centric design makes the report writing process more timely and coherent while reducing information loss during the iterative search process.\nL18: We demonstrate that our TTD-DR achieves state-of-the-art results on a wide array of benchmarks that require intensive search and multi-hop reasoning, significantly outperforming existing deep research agents.\nL19: Subjects:  | Computation and Language (cs.CL)\nL20: Cite as:  | cite25†arXiv:2507.16075 [cs.CL]\nL21:    | (or cite26†arXiv:2507.16075v1 [cs.CL] for this version)\nL22:    | cite27†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2507.16075†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL23: ## Submission history\nL24: \nL25: From: Rujun Ha